# #1434 r3: a call that RETURNS (mk) feeds a builtin that runs callbacks
# (sort_by's key) in the same expression. The trace stamp still held mk's
# `return q` (line 12) when sort_by entered, so each callback exit restored and
# taped line 12: after the last key return the stepper's next stop was 12, not
# the statement's line 15. [0g] steps the tape: after the last stop at line 9
# the next stop must be 15. LINE-NUMBER SENSITIVE.
define key(v) as:
    w is 0 - v
    return w
define mk(n) as:
    q is [[n, 2], key]
    return q
k is 60
loop while k > 0:
    x is len of (sort_by of (mk of k))
    k is k - 1
print of (what is x at 15)
